    {
      "sentence_id": 34,
      "text": "BEFORE  HONOURABLE MR. JUSTICE SOUMITRA SAIKIA  ORDER 11-12-2024 Heard Mr. T.H. Hazarika, learned counsel for the petitioners.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1602,
      "end": 1728,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "SOUMITRA SAIKIA",
          "label": "JUDGE",
          "start": 1633,
          "end": 1648
        },
        {
          "text": "11-12-2024",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 1656,
          "end": 1666
        },
        {
          "text": "T.H. Hazarika",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 1677,
          "end": 1690
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 35,
      "text": "Also heard Mr. H. Sarma,\nlearned Additional Senior Government Advocate, Assam for the respondent nos.3 & 4 and Ms. P.R.\nMahanta, learned Standing Counsel, Revenue and Disaster Management Department for the respondent nos. 1 & 2 and Ms. K. Phukan, learned CGC for the respondent no. 5 & 6.\n2] The grievance of the petitioners are that they were initially informed by the Deputy Commissioner, Kamrup (Metro) that the land belonging to the writ petitioners will be acquired by way of negotiated settlement as per the Page No.# 3/4 Government notification dated 07.03.2022.\nIn terms of this negotiation, a notice was published in newspapers including the Assam Tribune in its addition dated 07.12.2022 which reflected that the names of the petitioners along with their corresponding land proposed to be requisitioned by virtue of direct purchase method.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1729,
      "end": 2578,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "H. Sarma",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 1744,
          "end": 1752
        },
        {
          "text": "Assam",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 1801,
          "end": 1806
        },
        {
          "text": "P.R.\nMahanta",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 1844,
          "end": 1856
        },
        {
          "text": "K. Phukan",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 1965,
          "end": 1974
        },
        {
          "text": "Kamrup",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 2120,
          "end": 2126
        },
        {
          "text": "07.03.2022",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 2287,
          "end": 2297
        },
        {
          "text": "Assam Tribune",
          "label": "ORG",
          "start": 2380,
          "end": 2393
        },
        {
          "text": "07.12.2022",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 2416,
          "end": 2426
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 36,
      "text": "Subsequently,\nby order dated 24.01.2024 passed in LA case No.1 of 2024 the land of the petitioners were requisitioned under Section 3 (1) of the Assam Land (Requisition and Acquisition) Act, 1964 by the Page No.# 1/4 vs The State Of Assam And 5 Ors on 11 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/27761368/\n2",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 2579,
      "end": 2904,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "24.01.2024",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 2608,
          "end": 2618
        },
        {
          "text": "LA case No.1 of 2024",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 2629,
          "end": 2649
        },
        {
          "text": "Section 3 (1)",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 2703,
          "end": 2716
        },
        {
          "text": "Assam Land (Requisition and Acquisition) Act, 1964",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 2724,
          "end": 2774
        },
        {
          "text": "11 December, 2024",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 2831,
          "end": 2848
        },
        {
          "text": "Indian Kanoon",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 2849,
          "end": 2862
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 37,
      "text": "District Commissioner and Collector, Kamrup(M) District.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 2905,
      "end": 2961,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Kamrup(M) District",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 2942,
          "end": 2960
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 38,
      "text": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the land has already been requisitioned and the work is being carried out in full swing but no compensation till date has been paid to the petitioners in terms of the earlier commitment given by the Government for release of the payment in respect of acquiring the land through the direct purchase method.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 2962,
      "end": 3316,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3362947702407837
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 39,
      "text": "Being aggrieved, they have approached this Court.",
      "rhetorical_role": "FAC",
      "start": 3317,
      "end": 3366,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "facts",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.17437762022018433
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 40,
      "text": "3] Mr. H. Sarma, learned Additional Public Prosecutor, Assam, submits that any grievance in respect of the compensation is to be resolved by taking recourse of the statutory remedy prescribed under and therefore, the maintainability of the writ petition is doubtful.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ARG_PETITIONER",
      "start": 3367,
      "end": 3634,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "H. Sarma",
          "label": "OTHER_PERSON",
          "start": 3375,
          "end": 3383
        },
        {
          "text": "Assam",
          "label": "GPE",
          "start": 3423,
          "end": 3428
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "arguments",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1850566267967224
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 41,
      "text": "4] Having heard the learned counsel for the parties, issue Notice, returnable 2 (two) weeks.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 3635,
      "end": 3728,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 42,
      "text": "Since all the respondents are represented by their respective counsel, Notices are waived.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 3729,
      "end": 3820,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.10128635168075562
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 43,
      "text": "However,\nextra copies of the petition be furnished to the learned counsel for the respondents respectively within 3 (three) working days from today.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 3821,
      "end": 3969,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 44,
      "text": "5] Let the matter be listed again on 09.01.2025.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 3970,
      "end": 4019,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "09.01.2025",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 4008,
          "end": 4018
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.044853758066892624
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 45,
      "text": "6] Prayer for interim order as well as the question of maintainability of the  Page No.# 4/4 petition will be taken up for consideration on the next date fixed.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
